#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# revolution_plot3d

#% text
# `revolution_plot3d(f, [t, a, b])` draws the surface swept by the curve z = f(t), at distance t from the z axis, turned once about the axis.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is `image("path")`, a PNG with SVG and PDF copies next to it.

#% item
# A list of functions draws several surfaces.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A paraboloid:

#% cell
revolution_plot3d(t^2, [t, 0, 1])
#% output
#= image("revolution_plot3d.files/revolution_plot3d-1.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A vase:

#% cell
revolution_plot3d(sin(3t)/3 + t, [t, 0.1, 2])
#% output
#= image("revolution_plot3d.files/revolution_plot3d-2.svgz")

#% text
# Two surfaces:

#% cell
revolution_plot3d([t, 2 - t], [t, 0, 1])
#% output
#= image("revolution_plot3d.files/revolution_plot3d-3.svgz")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# Turned over a part of the circle, with a turn of the angle:

#% cell
revolution_plot3d(sqrt(t), [t, 0, 1], [p, 0, 3pi/2])
#% output
#= image("revolution_plot3d.files/revolution_plot3d-4.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `spherical_plot3d`, `parametric_plot3d`, `plot3d`
